Cell["\<\
Only the s = 1 row stays finite; the others grow without bound. The point r = \
2m lies at a finite proper distance (the integral of f^(\[Minus]s/2) dr \
converges there), so these are genuine curvature singularities.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5cd7f018-fdfa-489e-a09e-c5d7a733ba9a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
